title: MWSServerList/Environment

\whitespace trim
<$let env="$:/temp/TiddlyDesktop/MWS/Environment">
<$list filter="[<env>get[node-ok]!match[yes]]" variable="ignore">
<div class="td-mws-notice td-mws-notice-error">
<$list filter="[<env>get[node]!is[blank]]" variable="version" emptyMessage="""<strong>Node.js was not found.</strong> MWS needs Node.js 20 or newer on this computer to install and run local servers.""">
<strong>Node.js <<version>> is too old.</strong> MWS needs Node.js 20 or newer.
</$list>
<p>
<$button class="td-button td-mws-primary" message="tm-mws-install-node">Install Node.js automatically</$button>
&#32;downloads the current LTS version from nodejs.org into the ~TiddlyDesktop data folder (no administrator rights needed, nothing else on the computer is changed).
</p>
<$list filter="[<env>get[install-progress]!is[blank]]" variable="progress">
<p><em><$text text=<<progress>>/></em></p>
</$list>
<p>
Alternatively install it yourself from <a href="https://nodejs.org/" class="tc-tiddlylink-external">nodejs.org</a>, or set the Node.js folder under <$button class="tc-btn-invisible tc-tiddlylink" message="tiddlydesktop-add-wiki-url" param="backstage://$:/TiddlyDesktop/Settings">Settings</$button>, then&#32;
<$button class="td-button" message="tm-mws-check-environment">check again</$button>
</p>
</div>
</$list>
<div class="td-mws-environment">
Node.js: <$text text={{{ [<env>get[node]else[not found]] }}}/>
&#32;· npm: <$text text={{{ [<env>get[npm]else[not found]] }}}/>
&#32;· ssh: <$text text={{{ [<env>get[ssh]else[not found]] }}}/>
&#32;<$button class="tc-btn-invisible tc-tiddlylink" message="tm-mws-check-environment">(check again)</$button>
</div>
</$let>
